<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33110" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oscĭtātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		oscito, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an opening of the mouth wide</i>, <i>a
				gaping.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conchas pandentes sese quādam
					oscitatione,</span>”
				<i>a gaping</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 35, 54, § 107</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>a gaping</i>, <i>yawning</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 6, 5, § 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 4,
				20, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 2, 6,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sed Bruti senis oscitationes,</span>”
				<i>tediousnesses</i>, <i>tedious writings</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 9, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non ipse (judex) nostrā oscitatione
					solvatur,</span>”
				<i>by our languid speaking</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
